  "appeal_decision": null,
  "description": "Following separately applying for planning for the re-roofing and further exterior refurbishments on St Mary’s Court (PP-14115921), this application seeks further approval for the installation of Solar PV Panels on the church roof.\n \nThe proposal consists of the installation of 30 Solar PV panels on south facing roof, aimed at maximising available roof space. 13.65kW solar array. The site has preferable orientation and inclination making it very suitable.\n\nThis integration of modern technology into heritage fabric represents the future of heritage site preservation, with maximum energy saving and sustainability at its core, ensuring their continued status for future generations. It will save the equivalent of 5.8 tonnes of CO2 emissions in year one. The installation of the solar PV panels comfortably comply with local heritage policies. The existing Velux windows on the roof mean that the addition of the Solar PV Panels wont significantly alter the sites appearance from street view. Retaining the buildings aesthetic, and therefore historical significance and character.",
